# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository.
#
# This is not cosmetic. The repo is developed on Windows but built and run on Linux — both by
# the Docker build and on the VPS — and several files here are executed rather than read:
# `mod/gradlew` and the deploy scripts fail with a confusing "bad interpreter" error if their
# shebang line ends with CRLF. Pinning them avoids a class of bug that only appears after a
# checkout on the other platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Executed on Linux. Never CRLF, regardless of local git config.
*.sh text eol=lf
mod/gradlew text eol=lf

# Windows-only, and PowerShell is happiest with CRLF.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
mod/gradlew.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary — never touched, never diffed as text.
*.jar binary
*.png binary
*.schem binary
*.pdf binary
